# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Blorbmart web — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` (or set these in Vercel) and the bundled defaults in
# src/lib/config.ts stop being used. Every value here is public by design:
# Firebase web config and the VAPID public key ship inside the client bundle
# on every platform. Firestore rules and the backend's auth are the real
# boundary. Never put a service-account key or a Paystack secret here.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The API. Must be the host that is actually deployed — blorbmart.onrender.com
# answers 404 to every path, including /health.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://blorbmart-tr1i.onrender.com

# Firebase — matches DefaultFirebaseOptions.web in the app's
# lib/firebase_options.dart. The web build and the phone build must point at
# the same project or they see different catalogues.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyAGGDTIx4YY8_7cwuPBDkJV-plZpr-IhWs
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=blorbmart-b29b7.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=blorbmart-b29b7
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=blorbmart-b29b7.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_SENDER_ID=840596799490
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:840596799490:web:b4b2e30afc4efedbe6671b

# Web push certificate (public half of the VAPID pair). Issued per Firebase
# project, so this is the same key the rider app uses. Without it, push is a
# no-op and the rest of the app still works.
VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=BGVY6js1W1Fo9V9ZYLn3JRJSFQPZZQfkbq8s7qaNepfaCdqUrMQX6HBTLco-Ok-YOPe_blzFJo0yZly4BhY_K8U
